<h2>Practical Implementation</h2>
<p>Consider the mathematics of risk and reward. The Kelly Criterion defines the optimal fraction of a bankroll to risk on a given proposition. The formula is written plainly as f* = (bp - q) / b, where 'b' represents the decimal odds minus 1, 'p' is the probability of winning, and 'q' is the probability of losing. For instance, with odds of 2.00 (b=1) and a true win probability of 53%, the optimal stake is 6%. However, deploying the full Kelly fraction often results in unacceptable volatility, which is why professionals utilize Fractional Kelly.</p>
